        "comments": "The assembly daArtNorv1.hap1.1 is based on 43x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Haplotypic inversions are present on the following chromosomes: chromosome 1 between\n67.26-81.47Mb, chromosome 2 between\n180.36-196.97Mb, chromosome 5 between\n25.20-60.84Mb and chromosome 8 between\n43.65-73.45Mb.",
